Allow EIP197 inline/DDK crypto on BPI-R4 (and other filogic MT7988A boards)

CRYPTO_OFFLOAD_INLINE is gated on a list of board names, not on the SoC:

    depends on TARGET_mediatek_mt7988
            || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988a-rfb
            || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988d-rfb

Before eff13a547 (2025-02-18) the condition was TARGET_mediatek_mt7988,
a subtarget, so every MT7988A board matched.  The refactor replaced it with
MTK's two reference boards and nobody else's was ever added.

The gate is not a hardware one.  mt7988a-rfb and bananapi_bpi-r4 are the
same MT7988A silicon, and the crypto and pce nodes both live in the shared
mt7988a.dtsi with status = "okay":

    crypto@15600000  compatible = "inside-secure,safexcel-eip197b",
                                  "security-ip-197-srv"   <- MTK DDK binds here
    pce@15100000     compatible = "mediatek,pce"

Without this, kmod-crypto-eip-inline cannot be selected on a BPI-R4, and with
it neither kmod-crypto-eip-autoload nor the look-aside code, which is compiled
into the same crypto-eip-inline.ko (src/Makefile:17-19).  The whole MTK EIP
driver is unreachable and mainline safexcel is the only option.

Adds the standard BPI-R4 only, in their own style.  That is the board we test
on; the Pro 8X and the other variants are deliberately left out so this stays
the smallest possible change to someone else's feed.

A SoC-level condition would be the right upstream fix, not a device list.

--- a/feed/kernel/crypto-eip/Config.in
+++ b/feed/kernel/crypto-eip/Config.in
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 
 config CRYPTO_OFFLOAD_INLINE
 	bool "Inline Mode"
-	depends on TARGET_mediatek_mt7988 || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988a-rfb || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988d-rfb
+	depends on TARGET_mediatek_mt7988 || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988a-rfb || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_mediatek_mt7988d-rfb || TARGET_DEVICE_mediatek_filogic_DEVICE_bananapi_bpi-r4
 	select PACKAGE_kmod-crypto-eip-inline
 	select PACKAGE_kmod-crypto-eip-ddk
 	select PACKAGE_kmod-crypto-eip-ddk-ksupport
